cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "contract-patch-verify: an independent Lean witness-DAG oracle for CASSIE patch detection"
abstract: >
  A contract is what a transport layer and an interactor compose against, and this
  one is a second opinion rather than a shared definition: a Lean 4 witness-DAG
  oracle that verifies CASSIE patch detection without sharing code with the
  implementation it checks. Independence is the whole design. An oracle that
  imports the thing it is checking agrees with it by construction, so the two are
  held apart and only their outputs are compared.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fire/contract-patch-verify"
keywords:
  - lean4
  - formal-verification
  - property-based-testing
  - differential-testing

# What this repository is built on. Every entry is pinned in lake-manifest.json or
# vendored under vendor/, so this file states what that pin resolves to and why it is
# here -- a rev is a fact about a commit and not about what was wanted from it.
references:

  - type: software
    title: "plausible: property-based testing for Lean 4"
    authors:
      - name: "The Lean community"
    url: "https://github.com/leanprover-community/plausible"
    notes: >
      Pinned at a456461b. The randomised search under every property this oracle
      states; a witness DAG is only worth building if something tries to falsify it.

  - type: software
    title: "plausible-witness-dag: witness DAGs over plausible"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/fire/plausible-witness-dag"
    notes: >
      Pinned at 160b94c9. The DAG structure the oracle's verdicts are carried in, so a
      failure names the witnesses that produced it rather than only the property that broke.

  - type: software
    title: "lean-slang: Slang shader-language codegen from Lean"
    url: "https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/lean-slang"
    notes: "Vendored under vendor/lean-slang, as a lake path dependency rather than a fetched rev."

  - type: software
    title: "Geogram: a programming library of geometric algorithms"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lévy
        given-names: Bruno
    url: "https://github.com/BrunoLevy/geogram"
    notes: "Vendored under vendor/geogram, with Eigen and the CASSIE triangulation and curve-RDP sources beside it."
